# CODEOWNERS: INFORMATIONAL ROUTING ONLY (D-RD-01).
#
# Every agent pushes and reviews as the one shared account @SangeethNallamilli,
# so every entry names that account and the comment above each group names the
# ROLE that must review it. "Require review from Code Owners" stays OFF in
# branch protection: with one account, the PR author is the only code owner and
# GitHub never lets an author approve their own PR, so it would deadlock every
# merge. The enforced gate is the required `approval-check` job
# (.github/workflows/approval.yml), whose path rules live in
# .github/approval-policy.json. Keep the two in step: change both together.
#
# Code review: every PR needs one Code Reviewer (CR1 or CR2, routed by the TL);
# both CRs if INTERFACES.md changes or the PR has > 400 changed lines.

